// N97. TYPECHECK-ONLY project covering src/ AND scripts/.
//
// apps/api/tsconfig.json is the BUILD config and must stay exactly as it is.
// Its `rootDir: "src"` is load-bearing: `npm run build` is bare `tsc`, `outDir`
// is `dist`, and both package.json `start` and railway.json `startCommand` are
// `node dist/index.js`. Widening the base config's `include` to cover scripts/
// forces rootDir to widen with it, which relocates the emit to
// `dist/src/index.js` and ships a service that will not start.
//
// So the two concerns are split instead: the base config still emits, and this
// one only checks. `noEmit` is what makes the widened rootDir harmless here —
// nothing is written, so no output layout can change.
//
// Kept in sync by construction: this extends the base rather than restating it,
// so every compilerOption above rootDir/noEmit has exactly one definition.
{
  "extends": "./tsconfig.json",
  "compilerOptions": {
    "noEmit": true,
    "rootDir": "."
  },
  "include": ["src/**/*", "scripts/**/*"]
}
